                    {
                        "sense_id": "00e4557d-34ea-35d4-b3d0-06b3379362f2",
                        "entry_id": "1fe1a65c-561f-374e-bd86-c86f0cb22b18",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lack or absence of harmony; disharmony; (by extension) discord; chaos"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf1bc44f-a941-43cc-80ca-eec61c01bc7c",
                                "sense_id": "00e4557d-34ea-35d4-b3d0-06b3379362f2",
                                "text": "That unharmony between God and human life is a possible experience to human life, requires no argument, and that, as a fact of human knowledge, [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "189e9494-8f9f-426c-aea8-65841b286a30",
                                "sense_id": "00e4557d-34ea-35d4-b3d0-06b3379362f2",
                                "text": "Chaos is absolute unharmony, and unharmony must struggle for harmony."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "620847c8-b725-493f-abfa-4befb0345f6a",
                                "sense_id": "00e4557d-34ea-35d4-b3d0-06b3379362f2",
                                "text": "It is in the moments of unharmony that the possibilities for constituting oneself, for folding the force as it were (Deleuze 1995), exist."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
